{"chunk_id": "606c4912ee80", "text": "This section recounts the dark origin of Parashurama\u2019s wrath against the warrior caste. Renuka, wife of the sage Jamadagni, momentarily feels desire upon seeing King Chitraratha sporting in the water. Jamadagni, perceiving her lapse in chastity, orders his sons to kill her; only Rama obeys, beheading his mother. Pleased with his obedience, Jamadagni grants Rama boons, allowing Renuka and his brothers to be restored and the sin erased. Later, the arrogant sons of Kartavirya steal the sacred cow from the hermitage. Rama kills their mighty leader, but in revenge they murder Jamadagni while he is absorbed in penance. Grief\u2011stricken, Rama vows annihilation of the Kshatriyas, slaughtering them repeatedly and filling Samantapanchaka with lakes of blood before renouncing the earth and retiring to penance.\nParashurama obeys Jamadagni by killing and reviving his mother, later avenges his father's murder by exterminating the Kshatriya race repeatedly.\nThemes: filial obedience, wrath and vengeance, brahmin vs kshatriya conflict, divine boons and resurrection, cycle of violence", "vector": [0.019308704882860184, -0.02802962437272072, -0.02120223641395569, 0.004147104453295469, 0.00892094150185585, 0.022162338718771935, -0.02609608694911003, -0.014948244206607342, -0.037363942712545395, -0.03000316582620144, 0.03088325820863247, 0.015468298457562923, 0.007047410123050213, -0.00268861697986722, -0.014734888449311256, 0.009627682156860828, 0.04923186078667641, -0.009354320354759693, 0.042244456708431244, -0.012514653615653515, 0.0045571476221084595, 0.011561219580471516, -0.015721658244729042, 0.010321089066565037, -0.011767907999455929, 0.020442157983779907, 0.002046882640570402, -0.02645612508058548, 0.01075446791946888, -0.014801561832427979, -0.0323500819504261, -0.015254942700266838, 0.013468087650835514, -0.0035337063018232584, -0.032510098069906235, 0.025229329243302345, -0.0025502690114080906, -0.016975125297904015, -0.00108